WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.130
Three points.

2
00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:02.780
One, two.

3
00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:04.730
Four, eleven.

4
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.760
Nine, twenty-seven.

5
00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.870
On a coarse grid, they
look perfectly in line.

6
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.350
A thick ruler laid across
seems to cover all three.

7
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.090
Zoom out, and they still seem lined up.

8
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.910
But a drawing can only be so accurate.

9
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.250
Do these three points really
lie on one straight line?

10
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.860
And can one calculation settle
it, without a huge accurate plot?

11
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:30.130
In this mission, you'll find
the gradient between two points:

12
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.220
the change in y over the change in x.

13
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:37.360
And you'll learn that three points are
collinear exactly when the gradients between

14
00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:38.770
them are equal.

15
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.390
Your mission: decide whether these
three points lie on one straight line.
